I thought, MAYBE I'd be free from this horrible addiction...
check this out:
Level 30 Priest
AC: -17
HP: 278 (278)
Speed Boots
Grey Dragon Scale Mail
Gauntlets of Power
Nice full bag of holding
Basically unlimited blank scrolls and magic markers (I got bored of
curse-genociding Wraiths and Nurses)
Every intrinsic known to man except maybe disintegration resistance
+5 Excaliber (I suppose I could've enchanted it more, but I hate risking
vaporization)
tons of other stuff...

So I get to the castle level, and find a trapdoor in the first maze
section which drops me into Hell.  I wander around hell for a bit, and
discover that "Heavens to Betsy!  The Wizard of Yendor is RIGHT HERE!"
So without even going back up to do the castle, I just grab the amulet,
and scoot.  Of course the Wizard gets pissed, and comes after me full
force...after a couple of hairy moments I eventually paralize him at
the castle steps, and leave.  No sweat going up all the levels, I kill
him once more at level 1, and it's off to the endgame.  "No way I can
lose!" I'm thinking to myself...No problem, I'm killing off all the
Liches and dragons and stuff, still at max hp's and all that, and I
find this little moat.  Well, the only thing I DON'T have is a way
to cross water...but it doesn't seem to be a problem since there's a
little pathway right through it.  I search and find a secret door, I
open it, and something happens (I still don't know what) and it's as
if I hit <shift> down-arrow, right into the water.

"Killed by a Moat"
I think I'm going to cry.

